@* The body of a native dialog, and nothing else.

   Mounted as the root component of the WebView a native head puts inside its own dialog frame —
   the middle of an NSPanel sheet on macOS. It draws no title and no buttons, because those are the
   platform's and drawing them here is the bug docs/NATIVE-SHELL.md section 4 exists to prevent. *@
@implements IDisposable
@inject NativeDialogState State

@* Its own document — a native dialog's body is a separate WebView, so it needs its own copy of
   the symbols and its own copy of the platform's resolved colours. *@
<IconSprite />
<PlatformThemeSync />

<div class="surface">
    @if (State.Current is { } session)
    {
        <DialogContent @key="session" Session="session" Measure="true" />
    }
</div>

@code {
    protected override void OnInitialized() => State.Changed += OnChanged;

    void OnChanged() => InvokeAsync(StateHasChanged);

    public void Dispose() => State.Changed -= OnChanged;
}
